          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p>According to the question,</p>\n\n<p>Row 1: F, H, K, M, T</p>\n\n<p>Row 2: B, I, N, P, Q</p>\n\n<p>1) I sits at the middle of the row.</p>\n\n<p>2) No person sits to the left of P.</p>\n\n<p>3) M sits at extreme end but not placed behind P.</p>\n\n<p>4) N is neither a neighbour of Q nor B.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F17_Antesh_25-11-2020_Swati_D1.png\" style=\"width: 206px; height: 143px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>5) Q sits in front of F and is also a neighbour of B.</p>\n\n<p>6) One person sits between F and K.</p>\n\n<p>7) H is not a neighbour of F.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/12/F17_Antesh_25-11-2020_Swati_D2.png\" style=\"width: 207px; height: 147px;\" /></p>\nHence, &ldquo;Two&rdquo; persons sit between P and Q.",
